+# H10 fixture · browser activation
 
-This renamed Web plugin is valid on the host side but its browser bundle still
-registers a legacy identity. Exam material only — do not publish (`"private": true`).
+A renamed Web plugin. The host half is an ordinary cordis plugin (`apply` in
+`index.js`), mounted as a profile row by `cordis.patch.yml` through the
+`dsh.bundle.patch` manifest field. The browser half is declared by `dsh.client`
+(`platform: web`, `./client` export) and registers one web-client module; when
+the web composition activates it, it sets
+`document.documentElement.dataset.benchBrowserActivation = 'active'`.
+
+The harness keys each client graph row by package name, and the module system
+rejects a bundle that does not register that id (`client-modules: bundle …
+loaded without registering …`). The registration id in `client.js` therefore
+follows the package name through a rename; the pre-rename
+`@demo/dsh-bench-browser-activation-legacy` registration is retired, because a
+boot row can only request the package name.
+
+Exam material only — do not publish (`"private": true`).
